<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="section-label">Common questions about payment</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Quick answers.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Why Stripe? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Stripe is the standard payment processor for small agencies, and it handles card and ACH transactions on PCI-compliant infrastructure. The agency never sees or stores your card number on its end of the wire, since Stripe holds all payment information directly. Stripe also handles dunning, dispute resolution, and the international payment surface for Canadian clients.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Do I need to have signed the agreement before paying? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, the signed <a href="/agreement/" class="inline-link">service agreement</a> needs to be in place before the first payment runs. The agreement arrives by email as a Google Docs e-signature request after the discovery call, and once both signatures are in I send the link to this page so the first payment kicks the build off.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I switch from monthly to a one-time buyout later? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, you can. If at some point you would rather own the code outright, I am happy to quote a buyout, and the conversation tends to be a straightforward one. There is no penalty attached to asking, and the buyout amount is calculated against the months you have already paid.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I need a refund? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The refund posture is in the <a href="/agreement/" class="inline-link">service agreement</a> in plain language. The short version: if I have not started building yet and you change your mind within the first week, the first payment is refundable in full. After the build kicks off, refunds are handled on a case-by-case basis, and I would rather find a reasonable way forward than collect against a relationship that is not working.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Is the hourly link gated? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Soft-gated, yes. The hourly link is meant for clients who already have a written estimate from me and want to settle a block of hours, and it is not the right starting point for a new piece of work. If you do not have an estimate yet, send the request through the <a href="/ask/" class="inline-link">short ask form</a> first and I will scope the work and quote it before any payment changes hands.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

